The assert statements outputted are indicating the conditions mentioned in the comments. So, all the assert statements will look like this:

```cs
Debug.Assert(sum >= x && sum >= y);
Debug.Assert(New_arrListLastIndexOfX != Old_arrListCount);
```

Please note that the actual output might vary depending on the actual values of the variables in your code. Also, the "&&" operator is used to create a logical AND operation, which means both conditions have to be true. If any of the conditions is not true, then the code inside the Debug.Assert will not execute.
--------------------
Debug.Assert(!(New_Ret && New_arrListLastIndexOfX != Old_arrListCount));
</code>
--------------------
Debug.Assert(New_Ret == true && New_arrListLastIndexOfX != Old_arrListCount);
</code>
--------------------